  "items": [
    {
      "id": "https://deepmind.com/alphaproteo-v3",
      "url": "https://deepmind.com/alphaproteo-v3",
      "title": "AlphaProteo v3: 31% first-try binder success rate with conformer-aware design",
      "content_html": "<p>AlphaProteo v3 is DeepMind&#x27;s de novo protein binder design model. The v3 release adds a conformer-aware diffusion head that conditions on the target&#x27;s bound-state conformation (not just the apo structure), lifting first-try success rate from 18% (v2) to 31%.</p><p>On 12 therapeutic targets (PD-1, HER2, EGFRvIII, TNF\u03b1, IL-6R, VEGF, c-Met, BCL-2, KRAS-G12C, p53-R175H, Ras, \u03b2-amyloid), v3 designs binders with Kd &lt; 10 nM on 9/12 targets. Cryo-EM verifies the design matches the binding pose in 78% of cases (v2 was 71%).</p><p>Released as open weights on HuggingFace under CC-BY-NC 4.0. The 8,400-binder library from v3 is downloadable as PDB + paired Kd + cryo-EM structures.</p>",
      "summary": "AlphaProteo v3 is DeepMind's de novo protein binder design model. The v3 release adds a conformer-aware diffusion head that conditions on the target's bound-state conformation (not just the apo structure), lifting first-try success rate from 18% (v2) to 31%.",
      "date_published": "2026-12-10T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "DeepMind Isomorphic Sciences"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "Biology - De novo protein design",
        "DeepMind blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "AlphaProteo v3 binder library (8,400 designs \u00d7 12 targets)",
        "format": "PDB + CSV (Kd)",
        "size": "1.4 GB",
        "url": "https://github.com/alphaproteo/v3-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/bionemo-3",
      "url": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/bionemo-3",
      "title": "BioNeMo-3: 12B-param drug discovery FM with diffusion-based pose refinement",
      "content_html": "<p>BioNeMo-3 (12B params) is NVIDIA&#x27;s third-generation drug-discovery foundation model, released at SC26. Trained on 3.2B protein sequences + 940M structures + 180M ligand-binding pairs. Key upgrade: a diffusion-based pose refinement head (DockingFuser v2) that iteratively refines binding poses.</p><p>CASP17 GDT_TS 0.91 (beats AlphaFold 3&#x27;s 0.87 and ESM-4&#x27;s 0.92 by combining both architectures). DockingFuser v2 achieves 0.95 Top-1 pose accuracy on PDBbind-2026 (vs 0.92 in v1).</p><p>Available via NIM containers + NGC catalog. Free academic access; commercial via NVIDIA AI Enterprise. Includes a 10,000-GPU academic credit programme.</p>",
      "summary": "BioNeMo-3 (12B params) is NVIDIA's third-generation drug-discovery foundation model, released at SC26. Trained on 3.2B protein sequences + 940M structures + 180M ligand-binding pairs. Key upgrade: a diffusion-based pose refinement head (DockingFuser v2) that iteratively refines binding poses.",
      "date_published": "2026-11-20T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "NVIDIA BioNeMo team"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "Biology - Drug discovery FM",
        "NVIDIA blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "BioNeMo-3 model + DockingFuser v2 benchmark",
        "format": "Checkpoint + PDB + SDF",
        "size": "48 GB",
        "url": "https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/bionemo-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://deepmind.com/alphagenome-2",
      "url": "https://deepmind.com/alphagenome-2",
      "title": "AlphaGenome 2: whole-genome variant effect prediction at 1Mbp context",
      "content_html": "<p>AlphaGenome 2 is DeepMind&#x27;s foundation model for predicting the effects of genetic variants across the entire genome. The v2 release extends the context window from 100kbp to 1Mbp \u2014 long enough to capture enhancer-promoter loops and topologically-associating domains (TADs).</p><p>On the Enformer-2026 benchmark (variant effect prediction for 35 tissues), AlphaGenome 2 achieves Pearson r=0.81 (vs r=0.61 for Enformer 2021, r=0.71 for Borzoi 2024). The 1Mbp context matters most for distal enhancers (&gt;100kbp from promoter), where AlphaGenome 2&#x27;s lead over Enformer grows to 0.21 r-units.</p><p>Released as open weights (CC-BY-NC 4.0). Includes a unified API: given a VCF file, output predicted expression changes per tissue per variant.</p>",
      "summary": "AlphaGenome 2 is DeepMind's foundation model for predicting the effects of genetic variants across the entire genome. The v2 release extends the context window from 100kbp to 1Mbp \u2014 long enough to capture enhancer-promoter loops and topologically-associating domains (TADs).",
      "date_published": "2026-12-03T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "DeepMind Genomics"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "Genomics - Variant effect prediction",
        "DeepMind blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "Enformer-2026 benchmark (35 tissues \u00d7 1000 variants)",
        "format": "VCF + JSON",
        "size": "320 MB",
        "url": "https://github.com/alphagenome/2-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://mistral.ai/med-large",
      "url": "https://mistral.ai/med-large",
      "title": "Mistral Med-Large: open-weight 70B medical LLM (Apache 2.0)",
      "content_html": "<p>Mistral Med-Large is a 70B-parameter medical LLM fine-tuned from Mistral Large 3 on 14M de-identified clinical notes + 6M PubMed abstracts + 2M medical exam Q&amp;A (USMLE + MRCP + PLAB). It is the first fully open-weight medical LLM at this scale.</p><p>On the MedQA-USMLE benchmark, Mistral Med-Large achieves 89% (matching AMIE&#x27;s 85%, beating GPT-4o&#x27;s 73%). On the MultiMedQA suite (MedQA + PubMedQA + MedMCQA + MMLU-clinical), it scores 0.84 \u2014 beating the previous open-weight best (Meditron-3 70B) by 8 percentage points.</p><p>Released under Apache 2.0 \u2014 the first 70B medical LLM fully available for commercial use. Includes a 5-shot prompting protocol + RAG template for clinical guidelines.</p>",
      "summary": "Mistral Med-Large is a 70B-parameter medical LLM fine-tuned from Mistral Large 3 on 14M de-identified clinical notes + 6M PubMed abstracts + 2M medical exam Q&A (USMLE + MRCP + PLAB). It is the first fully open-weight medical LLM at this scale.",
      "date_published": "2026-11-25T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Mistral AI + Hugging Face"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "CS - Medical LLM",
        "Mistral AI blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "MultiMedQA benchmark (4 datasets \u00d7 1500 items each)",
        "format": "JSON",
        "size": "180 MB",
        "url": "https://github.com/mistralai/med-large-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://openai.com/sora-vision-medical",
      "url": "https://openai.com/sora-vision-medical",
      "title": "Sora-vision medical: video-input multimodal LLM for clinical video review",
      "content_html": "<p>Sora-vision medical is OpenAI&#x27;s multimodal LLM fine-tuned from Sora 2 for clinical video review. Inputs: endoscopy video, surgical video, echocardiogram loops, ultrasound sweeps. Outputs: timestamped findings, severity grading, recommended next steps.</p><p>On the OpenEndo-2026 benchmark (200 endoscopy videos \u00d7 5 findings each), Sora-vision medical achieves 0.87 mean average precision (mAP) \u2014 beating specialist models (Med-Gemini-Vid 0.74, General Sora 2 0.58). Mean time-to-first-finding: 4.2 seconds (vs 12.5s for a human endoscopist).</p><p>Stanford GI pilot (3-month, 4 clinics): flagged 23 polyps that the endoscopist missed in real-time (24% of total polyps found) \u2014 likely representing the difference between early-stage detection and progression to cancer.</p>",
      "summary": "Sora-vision medical is OpenAI's multimodal LLM fine-tuned from Sora 2 for clinical video review. Inputs: endoscopy video, surgical video, echocardiogram loops, ultrasound sweeps. Outputs: timestamped findings, severity grading, recommended next steps.",
      "date_published": "2026-12-15T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "OpenAI Health Sciences"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "CS - Medical video LLM",
        "OpenAI technical report"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "OpenEndo-2026 benchmark (200 videos \u00d7 5 findings)",
        "format": "MP4 + JSON",
        "size": "1.2 GB",
        "url": "https://github.com/openai/sora-vision-medical-2026"
      }
    },
